# Backend Guardrails

## API and Validation

- All new/updated endpoints should use route-level validation schemas.
- Keep response shape consistent (`message`, plus domain data fields).
- Preserve role checks with `requireRole(...)` and align with business policy.

## Data and Prisma

- Update [backend/prisma/schema.prisma](mdc:backend/prisma/schema.prisma) first for model changes.
- Add migrations for schema changes; do not rely on ad-hoc DB edits.
- Use Prisma constraints and explicit controller error mapping for expected conflicts.

## Logging and Errors

- Use structured logging via `req.log?.error(...)` in catches.
- Avoid leaking stack traces or raw Prisma internals to users.
- Keep user-facing error text actionable and short.
